e could argue that Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving may outweigh his moody/loner traits, but we lack crew cooperation evidence. Or we could argue that Candidate C's reliability and crew atmosphere may be stronger than B's communication issues. However we lack stress resilience and technical competence for C.\n\nGiven the panel's need for safety-critical, we need evidence across all criteria. B has evidence for reliability, stress resilience, technical competence. Communication concerns are present but perhaps manageable. D lacks reliability evidence, crew cooperation, stress resilience. A lacks many.\n\nThus likely maintain B.\n\nWe should reference the recent evidence: Agent 1's lack of reliability for A, Agent 2's lack of reliability for D, and earlier discussion about C lacking stress resilience and technical competence. So we can argue B remains best.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills. Also mention concerns: pretentious, wrong tone.\n\nThus we can state we keep vote for Candidate B.\n\nWe must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft."}
